      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator has the form \\( f(\\frac{\\pi}{6} + h) - f(\\frac{\\pi}{6}) \\) with \\( f(x) = \\tan x \\), because \\( f(\\frac{\\pi}{6}) = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Sqrt",
               3
            ],
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "So the function is \\( f(x) = \\tan x \\) and the base point is \\( x = \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            "Pi",
            6
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The limit is the definition of \\( f'(\\frac{\\pi}{6}) \\), and \\( f'(x) = \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Power",
               [
                  "Tan",
                  "x"
               ],
               2
            ],
            1
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluate: \\( f'(\\frac{\\pi}{6}) = \\frac{4}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            4,
            3
         ]
      }
